Z||000002||Songman||06-27-2001||08:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierowrecker:<BR><B> WHAT GAS CRISIS???!!!???<BR>The powers that be in office AROUND THE WORLD have scaled back production to boost the prices...<BR>crash...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Exactly! And not to mention playing footsies under the table with the Arabs at our expense. They need out imports a lot more than we need their oil in the first place... and we certainly don't need it enough to be held hostage at whatever price they set.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||06-28-2001||09:28 AM||||Supply and demand works...<P>The spot price for unleaded gas on the NYMEX hit a 17 month low yesterday. Gasoline demand is nearly 5% lower than this period a year ago. Why...prices that neared $2.50 per gallon this spring resulted in less driving and inventories have been building.<P>Lower prices (they've fallen nearly 60 cents per gallon here in the last 2 months) will stimulate demand and gas will rise again by Labor Day, but the $3 per gallon predictions will fail to come to pass this year.<P>Crude futures are also at their lowest levels since early 2000.<P>Market forces work...||||reg||1
